{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"The git sensor's one sweep (brick 4; contract kind git_state): reads the dev.git registry (runtime/dev/repos.json), runs one `status --porcelain=v2 --branch` per repo through dev.git.read, and emits perceptions only on EDGES - HEAD moved, branch switched, clean<->dirty crossing, ahead/behind change, merge/rebase/cherry-pick appearing or clearing. Emitted envelopes bind the claims whose {repo,path} sources name the repo, stale by working-tree byte compare. State persists at runtime/agent/git_sense.json, so a restart announces a standing dirty/mid-merge condition once instead of silently re-seeding. No .git mtime gate on purpose: worktree edits never touch .git, so a gate would miss exactly the clean->dirty crossing. The tailer loop calls this every ~30s; calling it deliberately is the test surface.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::command::Command;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;","params":[],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"tlurvg1a0245e69c0t1","readers":[],"time":1787316611456,"username":"system","writers":[]}